# `${2:-0}`/`${3:-0}` substituted 0 for an EMPTY count, so `0 - 0 -eq 0` passed
# on a file that EXISTS — measured rc=0. Worse than the absent-file case it was
# written to catch, because nothing looks wrong. Both operands are now refused
