# FLOOR_shell 996 -> 998 (#135 + #134's reporting half, addressed in PR #132).
# #135: all 13 mktemp calls in base-gate.sh were unchecked. On failure the
# variable stayed EMPTY, the redirection failed, and the classifier read $? as
# 1 with no tree sha -- the rc-1-no-sha branch. MEASURED at HEAD as uid 1000
# against a 0500 TMPDIR, full output:
#   mktemp: failed to create file via template '...': Permission denied
#   base-gate.sh: line 184: : No such file or directory
#   base-gate: merge-tree could not read an object for b903f32b..b903f32b -
#     the repository is incomplete (a truncated or shallow fetch takes exactly
#     this shape) ...
# Two defects in three lines: a raw bash error as operator guidance, and a
# confident diagnosis of a fetch that is fine. rc was already 2, so rc alone
# proves nothing -- what changed is WHICH cause it names, and that is what the
# CONTROL pins.
# THE SUBSHELL IS THE TRAP: `X="$(_mk foo)"` runs _mk in a subshell, so a die
# there exits THAT shell. Status propagates to the assignment, so every call
# site carries `|| exit 2`.
# Mutation, restored byte-identical (cmp): reverting all 13 sites to the
# inline unchecked form -- the TRUE pre-fix shape -- reds BOTH #135 cases in
# the bash suite. An earlier, weaker mutation (reverting only _mk's body) left
# the call-site guard catching it and the CONTROL stayed green; that was a
# mutation too weak to test what it claimed, caught before it shipped.
# #134's reporting half: the summary now prints a ROSTER of the skipped case
# titles, BELOW the marker line and never appended to it (gate-suite.sh:109
# anchors `^== summary: ... ==$`; appending fails the rung as a missing
# marker). A skip here is a property the executor cannot exhibit -- root
# bypasses the write bit, so every chmod-000/500 case is unexhibitable as uid
# 0 -- which is correct and unavoidable. What was not correct is a run saying
# "998 cases, slack 0" while 14 properties went untested. The non-root CI
# parity job, #134's other option, is NOT done here.
# Measured both ways, executor-invariant as #109 requires:
#   uid 0    -> 984 passed, 0 failed, 14 skipped = 998
#   uid 1000 -> 996 passed, 0 failed,  2 skipped = 998

